---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Button from '@/components/Button.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/site.config';

const tools = ['ServiceNow', 'JavaScript', 'Python', 'Power Query M', 'DAX', 'REST APIs'];
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={`A bit about ${SITE.name} and how they work.`}>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-16 pb-24 sm:pt-24">
    <p class="text-ink-soft mb-6 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase">About</p>

    <h1 class="font-display text-ink max-w-xl text-3xl font-medium sm:text-4xl">
      {SITE.role}
    </h1>

    <div class="prose prose-sm sm:prose-base mt-8 max-w-xl">
      
      <p>
        I build ServiceNow solutions that turn operational problems into practical products people can actually use and maintain.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most of my work sits at the intersection of development, IT asset management, automation, data, and user experience. I create applications, integrations, workflows, dashboards, and self-service tools that help organizations answer important questions: What technology do we own? Who is responsible for it? Where is it? And what needs to happen next?
      </p>
      <p>
        I like to start with the smallest useful version of a solution. That might be one workflow, one integration, one data gap, or one manual process that should not be manual anymore. I focus on making that first version reliable and useful, then improve and expand it over time.
      </p>
      <p>
        That approach has shaped projects such as hardware warranty integrations, asset lifecycle automation, Employee Center experiences, operational scorecards, and custom ServiceNow applications.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before focusing on ServiceNow development, I worked across systems administration, enterprise mobility, data, and IT operations. That background helps me think beyond the immediate request. I care about the entire product, including the data model, business process, security, automation, reporting, and the experience of the person using it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside of ServiceNow, I enjoy building web applications, experimenting with new ideas, and writing about the solutions, patterns, and lessons I pick up along the way.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10">
      <p class="text-ink-soft mb-3 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase">Tools</p>
      <ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        {
          tools.map((tool) => (
            <li class="border-line text-ink-soft rounded-full border px-3 py-1 font-mono text-xs">
              {tool}
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>

    <Button href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/eric-a-perez" variant="ghost" class="mt-10">Connect →</Button>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
